  "record_only": {
    "article_framing": [
      {
        "item": "Article abstract lists the final assessment as salicylate overdose with bezoar and salicylate toxicity.",
        "source_section": "Abstract",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "The report's stated objective is an unusual clinical course and CT failure to detect a gastric pharmacobezoar.",
        "source_section": "Abstract, Discussion, Conclusions",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      }
    ],
    "treatments_and_procedures": [
      {
        "item": "Initial interventions included glucose and bicarbonate infusions, multiple activated charcoal doses, intubation, emergent hemodialysis, and later CRRT.",
        "source_section": "Abstract, Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "The article reports 3 additional activated charcoal doses at 50 mg every 4 hours; this unit is transcribed as stated.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "Whole-bowel irrigation was given on day 4.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "Endoscopy on hospital day 5 found red blood throughout the stomach and a packet/paper wrapped around pills measuring 8-10 cm in the stomach body; retrieval was partially successful.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "Repeat endoscopy showed gastric mucosal bleeding, charcoal, and additional pill remnants, followed by cold-saline gastric lavage totaling 4 L.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      }
    ],
    "treatment_response_and_late_course": [
      {
        "item": "After initial dialysis, salicylate decreased to 400 mcg/mL and rebounded to 694 mcg/mL 6 hours later.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "Despite CRRT, salicylate levels later rebounded to 1005 mcg/mL.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "By day 4, salicylate levels rose to 491 mcg/mL, prompting continued hemodialysis with CRRT between intermittent sessions.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "After the second endoscopy and gastric lavage, salicylate levels declined continuously by hospital day 7.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      }
    ],
    "late_imaging_and_complications": [
      {
        "item": "Hospital day 3 CT abdomen/pelvis with IV and oral Gastrografin contrast showed moderate bibasilar pneumonia concerning for aspiration, small right upper-quadrant ascites, distended gallbladder with mild biliary ductal distention, and no gastric foreign body.",
        "source_section": "Case Report, Figure 1 legend",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "The hospital course was complicated by MSSA pneumonia.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "MRI brain was unrevealing; EEG showed moderate-to-severe encephalopathy without epileptiform discharges or electrographic seizures.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "Before repeat endoscopy, fresh frozen plasma and vitamin K were given for coagulopathy.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      },
      {
        "item": "On day 9, oliguria with acute kidney injury occurred in the setting of volume overload; nephrology was concerned for toxic tubular necrosis.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      }
    ],
    "outcome": [
      {
        "item": "Family deferred another planned hemodialysis session on day 10, pursued palliative care the next day, and the patient died after extubation.",
        "source_section": "Case Report",
        "use_in_ranking": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "extraction_caveats": [
    "Rankable observations were limited to demographics, risk context, initial ED presentation, initial laboratory and early objective studies. Post-intervention salicylate kinetics, endoscopic findings, late imaging, complications, treatment response, and outcome were placed in record_only.",
    "The source reports ammonia as 17 mcmol/L; this extraction stores the unit as micromol_per_L while preserving the article text in source_text_value.",
    "The source text reports activated charcoal dosing as 50 mg every 4 hours; this appears unusually low for activated charcoal but is retained verbatim in record_only."
